      'angiotensin ii is a powerful arteriolar vasoconstrictor it also stimulates the adrenal cortex to release aldosterone which makes the distal tubule reabsorb sodium and water and excrete potassium it stimulates adh release and thirst and constricts the efferent arteriole to protect gfr the net result is higher blood pressure and more retained fluid',
